  "style": {
    "name": "The Gate of the Sunwardens — Temple Facade",
    "rationale": "Kept the terracotta/teal/gold/blackstone split-complementary palette and rebuilt the facade as one bonded plane: a true round-arched vault (stepped teal voussoir ring, gold keystone, gold sunburst rays on the dark soffit), engaged piers with blackstone pilaster strips, gold-framed teal relief panels carrying gold figures, dark niches with gold sills, a layered gold/teal entablature with a dentil frieze, and a five-panel attic under a stepped gold-capped crenellated crown. Every wide field now carries banding or relief."
